WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:21.521
I was trying to think up a
name for a fantasy world that

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:23.481
might’ve been created by children,

00:00:23.481 --> 00:00:26.067
and what I came up
with was Boo’ya Moon,

00:00:26.067 --> 00:00:28.611
which sounds like a
childhood place to me.

00:00:29.571 --> 00:00:32.866
It’s a place that’s supposed
to be very, very beautiful

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:35.535
and at the same time, very dangerous,

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:39.330
where time doesn’t run the
way that it does on earth.

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.084
I wanted it to feel like
the inside of a dream

00:00:43.084 --> 00:00:44.753
that’s actually become real.

00:00:46.921 --> 00:00:50.383
Boo’ya Moon is part of that, you know,
sort of Stephen King multiverse.

00:00:50.925 --> 00:00:55.513
It is a place that was a bit
of a salvation for Scott and

00:00:55.513 --> 00:00:57.682
also a desperate necessity.

00:01:00.643 --> 00:01:02.187
You could almost call it a purgatory.

00:01:02.187 --> 00:01:04.355
There are people that
get kind of stuck there.

00:01:04.355 --> 00:01:07.358
It’s also a place that people
retreat from the world.

00:01:08.359 --> 00:01:09.986
That’s the place where
she finds her sister.

00:01:13.782 --> 00:01:17.702
All this works in a very symbolic way,
in a very metaphorical way,

00:01:17.702 --> 00:01:21.331
because even though
these worlds of fantasy are

00:01:21.331 --> 00:01:24.375
very fantastical and non-real,

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:29.464
they do represent certain
desires and illusions

00:01:29.464 --> 00:01:31.925
and situations that we
experience as humans.

00:01:33.718 --> 00:01:35.553
The whole interesting
thing about Boo’ya Moon

00:01:35.553 --> 00:01:38.181
is Stephen King’s absolutely
adamant it’s real.

